  "brief": "`intervals` holds closed intervals `{start, end}`, sorted by start, that do not overlap. Write `insert_interval(intervals, add)`. It adds the closed interval `add` and joins every interval it overlaps or touches. Return the list sorted by start.",
  "constraints": [
    "The list may be empty. Intervals that share an end point join: `{1, 2}` and `{2, 6}` give `{1, 6}`.",
    "$O(n)$ time is the target. Sorting the whole list again is allowed but not needed.",
    "Each test has a 5-second limit."
  ],
  "hint": "Copy the intervals that end before `add` starts. Then widen `add` over every interval that starts at or before its end. Finally copy the rest.",
