  "how": "Submit runs 13 hidden tests. Each answer must equal the expected value.",
  "solution": "#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n\nstd::vector<std::vector<int>> insert_interval(std::vector<std::vector<int>> intervals, std::vector<int> add) {\n    std::vector<std::vector<int>> out;\n    size_t i = 0;\n    int s = add[0], e = add[1];\n    while (i < intervals.size() && intervals[i][1] < s) out.push_back(intervals[i++]);\n    while (i < intervals.size() && intervals[i][0] <= e) {\n        s = std::min(s, intervals[i][0]);\n        e = std::max(e, intervals[i][1]);\n        ++i;\n    }\n    out.push_back({s, e});\n    while (i < intervals.size()) out.push_back(intervals[i++]);\n    return out;\n}\n",
  "notes": [
    "Intervals that end before `add` starts come first and are copied.",
    "Every interval that starts at or before the growing end is absorbed into `add`.",
    "The three loops share one index, so the work is $O(n)$."
  ]
